FSR 4.1 Lite 2.0 and later:
- bin/7zz is 7-Zip 25.01 for Linux x64 (7zzs, static) by Igor Pavlov, unmodified, under the GNU LGPL with the unRAR
  restriction (bin/7zz-License.txt). Source: https://github.com/ip7z/7zip and https://www.7-zip.org.
- OptiScaler (GPL-3.0, cdozdil and contributors) is not included. The plugin downloads the newest nightly build from
  https://github.com/optiscaler/OptiScaler-nightly at setup, unmodified; its source is at
  https://github.com/optiscaler/OptiScaler.
- AMD's FSR 4 files (amdxcffx64.dll, amdvkffx64.dll) are not included. The plugin downloads AMD's signed files,
  unmodified, from https://github.com/db1522/fsr4-files at setup.
- shim/ (LGPL-2.1+) is no longer part of the plugin as of 2.0.
- compat.json is a snapshot of each game's name, status and working upscaler inputs from OptiScaler's community
  Compatibility List (https://github.com/optiscaler/OptiScaler/wiki/Compatibility-List), made by scripts/compat.py.
  All credit to the OptiScaler community who keep it.
- REFramework (MIT, praydog) is not included. For the Capcom RE Engine games OptiScaler needs it in, the plugin
  downloads the newest nightly from https://github.com/praydog/REFramework-nightly, unmodified, and uses its dinput8.dll;
  its source is at https://github.com/praydog/REFramework.
